  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(\\mathrm{x})= \\begin{cases}(1+\\mathrm{ax})^{1 / \\mathrm{x}} & , \\quad \\mathrm{x} \\lt 0 \\\\ 1+\\mathrm{b} & , \\quad \\mathrm{x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{(\\mathrm{x}+4)^{1 / 2}-2}{(\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{c})^{1 / 3}-2} & ,\\end{cases}$<br/>be continuous at $x=0$. Then $e^a b c$ is equal to"
